      "title": "Latest quarter",
      "description": "Federal Reserve Z.1. The HOUSEHOLD share leads because it is the only figure here comparable across the whole history -- the total's population changed, and the second tile says by how much. Not FINRA's margin debt: $742bn against FINRA's $1,502bn at the same quarter, a ratio that drifts rather than scales, because the Fed's 'Security brokers and dealers' is a national-accounts sector and the concept includes other receivables. Quarterly, published about ten weeks after quarter end, so it describes a quarter already over: a regime measure, never a timing one.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "frser-sqlite-datasource",
            "uid": "offchart"
          },
          "queryType": "table",
          "rawQueryText": "SELECT household_pct_of_equities AS 'Household margin, share of their equities', pct_aggregate_hedge_funds AS 'Hedge funds as share of the total', broker_receivables AS 'Total customer receivables', household_margin_from_banks AS 'Household margin owed to banks' FROM board_leverage ORDER BY ts DESC LIMIT 1",
          "queryText": "SELECT household_pct_of_equities AS 'Household margin, share of their equities', pct_aggregate_hedge_funds AS 'Hedge funds as share of the total', broker_receivables AS 'Total customer receivables', household_margin_from_banks AS 'Household margin owed to banks' FROM board_leverage ORDER BY ts DESC LIMIT 1",
